<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marchand-Dessalines</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marchand</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marchand-Dessalines is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artibonite">Artibonite</a> valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a> made the capital of his empire after independence in 1804. He surrounded it with a ring of forts on the hills, such as Fort Fin-du-Monde, as a refuge against any French attempt at reconquest. After his assassination in 1806 the capital moved away, and the town was later renamed in his honour.</p></div>
